        "feedback": {
          "grade": "Incorrect",
          "result": "Incorrect",
          "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{y}^{2}\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2y[{\\int }_{y}^{2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2y\\cdot {[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{x=y}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2y\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{y}]\\text{ }\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2-y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[2y-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =(4-2)-(2-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
